# Contract first

`api/rest/v1/openapi.yaml` is the source of truth. The order is always: edit the contract →
regenerate → implement the handler.

```bash
cd internal/ui/api/v1/spec
oapi-codegen -old-config-style -package spec -generate types,skip-prune -o types.gen.go ../../../../../api/rest/v1/openapi.yaml
oapi-codegen -old-config-style -package spec -generate server  -o server.gen.go ../../../../../api/rest/v1/openapi.yaml
```

Use the generator version that matches the header of the existing `*.gen.go` files (v2.5.0);
the `go install ...@v2.4.0` line in `generator.go` is stale.

- Never hand-edit `internal/ui/api/v1/spec/*.gen.go`.
- Regeneration can surface drift accumulated earlier — optional contract fields become
  pointers. Fix the handler; do not bend the contract back to match old generated code.
- Every operation must document a `429` response; a test counts them.
- Contract text, descriptions and YAML comments are English.

# Tokens and limits

Anonymous callers get 10 requests per minute per IP; callers with `X-Token` get their plan
quota. The token is not validated yet, and that stays inside the handler package: a test
keeps wording like "not validated" or "arbitrary string" out of the contract.

Details: `.ai/conventions.md`.
